{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/78","id":4958059491,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUJ8YLs8AAAABJ4X74w","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/78","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/78.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/78.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/issues/78","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/78/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/78/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/issues/78/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/statuses/1fb1c6ea077fd260c373434c1a3c368a7952defd","number":78,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: compile finite native routes within CDN rule bounds","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?[query-redacted]","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Real native preview and stable A/B delivery maps contain 178 exact routes, exceeding the adapter's 50 literal-rule cap. This compiles larger maps into bounded finite rewrite expressions using only proven snapshot, public alias and fixed snapshot-site prefix relationships. Both retained native generations produce 17 rules, longest 1,017 bytes, with every original URI and target preserved. Tables with at most 50 unique routes keep their original serialized rules and order.\n\nThe compiler enumerates escaped alternatives in one capture with an absolute end anchor, caps each expression at 1,024 bytes and the domain at 50 rules, and keeps unknown mappings literal. Existing SDK configuration checks still refuse any required deletion before writes. The frozen public fixture binds the real native route/object facts and original source documents; SDK transport tests verify complete readback, A/B source ConfigId reuse and the two changed targets.\n\nTests were written and run red before implementation. An escaped-prefix boundary-test correction happened before implementation and both red outputs are retained. First validation passed all 34 SDK tests (original 22 unchanged plus 12 new), 10 input contracts, four repository contracts, and the full default suite (580 passed, one existing local RPM-tool skip). Independent Spec review found zero issues. Standards found no hard-rule violation and one P3 duplication suggestion; the two short wire constructors are retained with documented rationale and byte/order regression coverage. Independent finite-map and socket-guarded SDK probes passed.\n\nOnly five files change; provider AST outside compile_rewrites, workflows, tool locks, signing/channel controls, producers and native acceptance drivers remain unchanged. Exact-head Linux CI is pending. These results prove finite offline representation and SDK serialization, not live Alibaba PCRE/query behavior, all-object SDK integration, CDN cache propagation or public release acceptance. Stable remains disabled; no provider resources, production credentials, activation or publication are included.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T20:40:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T20:40:50Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5f597518d8c4722f8f971b6fe55e10ed7f8b539f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/native-route-compiler","ref":"codex/native-route-compiler","repo":{"id":1352603694,"node_id":"R_kgDOUJ8YLg","name":"packages","full_name":"WuKongIM/packages","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?[query-redacted]","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Signed APT and RPM repositories for WuKongIM","homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":1,"open_issues":1,"size":1257,"default_branch":"main","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_discussions":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pushed_at"